Temporary: say where a bubble's touch went and why the bubble closed.

The Web Bluetooth device chooser draws, lists devices and takes the keyboard,
but no touch anywhere inside it reaches it: a tap on its own title -- inside
the bubble, on nothing interactive -- closes it and requestDevice() rejects
with "NotFoundError: User cancelled the requestDevice() chooser". The
geolocation permission prompt, in the same session and at the same
`dispatch_target_`, receives its taps normally.

Measured on device before writing this, so the following are not open
questions: the ozone layer hands both bubbles to logical window 1 (bubbles get
no logical window of their own on this port, so `target=1` is what a working
bubble looks like too); the page never changes visibility while the chooser is
up, so LocationBarBubbleDelegateView's OnVisibilityChanged is not closing it;
and the two bubbles are created with the same anchor state (null), the same
parent window, and the same z-order sublevel.

What is left is above ozone and inside Views/aura, where reading has not
settled it. Four probes, all LOG(WARNING) so they land in hilog under the
Chromium tag, all behind BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS):

  * CreateBubbleWidget records what each bubble asked for, so the chooser and
    the permission prompt can be compared field by field rather than by
    reading the two call sites.
  * WindowTargeter::FindTargetForEvent records which aura window a touch press
    actually resolved to. This is the one measurement that separates "the
    event never reached the bubble" from "it reached the bubble and something
    inside rejected it".
  * OnBubbleWidgetActivationChanged records activation transitions, with the
    bubble's screen bounds -- which also answers whether the chooser's widget
    is as wide as it is drawn, since it renders clipped off the right edge.
  * Widget::CloseWithReason records the reason. BubbleDialogDelegate closes on
    deactivation with kLostFocus specifically, so this distinguishes that path
    from every other way the widget could be going away.

Remove once the chooser is fixed. Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-bubble-input-diagnostics.patch

